# PING — reflector to client keepalive.
#
# Source: "M17 Internet Protocol (IP) Networking", "Control Packets",
# Table 31 "Bytes of PING packet".
#
#   bytes 0-3   50 49 4E 47   Magic, ASCII "PING"
#   bytes 4-9   00 00 00 27 E8 ED
#                             6-byte 'From' callsign "including module in last
#                             character (e.g. "A1BCD D")" (Table 31). Here the
#                             encoded text is "M17 A" — reflector "M17",
#                             space, module 'A' — base-40 value 0x27E8ED.
#
# Total 10 bytes: unlike ACKN/NACK, PING does carry the address field.
50494E47 00000027E8ED
